  "contracts": {
    "numeric": "exact against bloom::runtime::unpackDisplaySignal: the Display codes are whole-number arithmetic, and code / 1023 and alpha / 255 are built by integer long division with round to nearest even, so every float equals the IEEE binary32 quotient of the CPU reference on every device",
    "dispatch": "one invocation per pixel, flattened row-major into 256-wide workgroups (gl_NumWorkGroups.x * 256 is the row stride); bindings 1 to 3 of the set are not read",
    "use": "the float signal picture of a shown frame for the scope measure (docs/architecture/scopes.md); it is never presented or exported"
